{"base_rate":0.5722222222222222,"brier":0.21618555555555555,"bss":0.11683116883116884,"bss_hi":0.24330052149473944,"bss_lo":-0.016544871409399566,"chart":{"base":[556.7,214.3],"fp":[205.0,187.0],"note":{"base":"skill 0.12 — higher than 18% of cities","fp":"low end -1pp, high end +20pp","rel":"promised 21% → rained 19%; promised 99% → rained 81%"},"rel":"194.7,382 423.6,270 591.6,218.5 683.3,114.1"},"country":"CO","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve"],"ece":0.1498888888888889,"ess":237.076736183522,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Medellin</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Medellin rain forecast is only marginally better than quoting the long-run average, though 5 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (100%), believe about\n<b>81%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(13%), there is still roughly a <b>13%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 540 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-03-23. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nthe station, 3.5 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.12, ranked 177 of\n216 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(129&ndash;192) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>13%</td><td class='num'><b>13%</b></td><td class='num'>53</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>29%</td><td class='num'><b>25%</b></td><td class='num'>55</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>48%</td><td class='num'><b>40%</b></td><td class='num'>53</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>66%</td><td class='num'><b>51%</b></td><td class='num'>55</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>79%</td><td class='num'><b>50%</b></td><td class='num'>52</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>89%</td><td class='num'><b>65%</b></td><td class='num'>51</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>95%</td><td class='num'><b>83%</b></td><td class='num'>52</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>100%</td><td class='num'><b>81%</b></td><td class='num'>169</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">5 of 8 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Medellin</b> <span class=\"muted\">Colombia</span></p>\n  <div class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag bad\">Barely beats the average</span><details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What does this label mean?\" title=\"What does this label mean?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>Compared with a simple guess: saying &ldquo;57% chance of rain&rdquo; every day, because it rains here on 57% of days.</p><p>The forecast did only slightly better. The difference is within the margin of error.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details>\n    <span class=\"muted\">5 points off by more than chance</span></div>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score<details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What is the skill score?\" title=\"What is the skill score?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>How much better the forecast is than that simple guess. 0 means no better, 1 means perfect, below 0 means worse. Day-ahead rain forecasts usually score 0.3 to 0.5.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details></dt><dd>0.12</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>129&ndash;192\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 216</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>540 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Medellin &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Medellin\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"102.48377358490566,299.58490566037733 161.56109090909092,229.78181818181818 228.12037735849057,155.35849056603774 293.056,97.41818181818178 338.9534615384615,53.0 372.504705882353,32.274509803921546 395.93384615384616,18.0 410.5337278106509,18.0 410.5337278106509,24.461538461538453 395.93384615384616,60.0 372.504705882353,89.37254901960785 338.9534615384615,136.99999999999997 293.056,183.45454545454547 228.12037735849057,251.50943396226415 161.56109090909092,315.8181818181818 102.48377358490566,361.39622641509436\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"173.71111111111114\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"173.71111111111114\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"102.48377358490566,333.92452830188677 161.56109090909092,289.3454545454546 228.12037735849057,237.77358490566036 293.056,196.69090909090912 338.9534615384615,200.0 372.504705882353,146.47058823529412 395.93384615384616,81.0 410.5337278106509,86.9230769230769\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 13%&amp;#10;It rained 13% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 53 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"102.48377358490566\" cy=\"333.92452830188677\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 29%&amp;#10;It rained 25% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 55 days&amp;#10;